User-entered custom ingredients were not normalized to lowercase, creating inconsistencies with predefined ingredients (which are already lowercase) and potential duplicate entries with different casing.

## Changes

- Modified `addIngredient` function in `ProfileSetup.tsx` to normalize custom ingredient input via `.toLowerCase()` before saving to `hatedIngredients` or `favoriteIngredients` lists

```typescript
const addIngredient = (
  value: string,
  list: string[],
  setList: (list: string[]) => void,
  setValue: (val: string) => void,
) => {
  const normalized = value.trim().toLowerCase();
  if (normalized && !list.includes(normalized)) {
    setList([...list, normalized]);
    setValue("");
  }
};
```

This ensures case-insensitive consistency across all ingredient storage and matching operations.

